# The changelog is one file per 0.Y series (doc/changelog/vX.Y.md) behind an
# index (doc/changelog/CHANGELOG.md). Both are append-only and both are
# named: [Unreleased] moved into the series file being written, so a pattern
# naming only CHANGELOG.md would leave the one file branches actually append
# to on the default three-way merge.
#
# The pattern is NOT the whole directory. A union merge cannot conflict --
# git keeps both sides of every overlapping hunk and marks nothing -- which
# is right for a log and wrong for prose. doc/changelog/CONVENTIONS.md is
# prose, and no gate in this repo reads it outside its changelog-categories
# marker block, so a union-merged duplicate paragraph there would ship
# unremarked. `doc/changelog/*.md` would have covered it; `v[0-9]*.md` names
# the series files and nothing else.
doc/changelog/CHANGELOG.md merge=union
doc/changelog/v[0-9]*.md merge=union
